                                            "figuratively",
                                            "literally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5506479-f129-40a0-a0ec-d0029a9d6642",
                                                "sense_id": "99be67b5-e891-3967-b412-32e407480ce5",
                                                "text": "hit the sack"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d0150a4-2a8b-422e-b254-fcba53e6ebbc",
                                                "sense_id": "99be67b5-e891-3967-b412-32e407480ce5",
                                                "text": "in the sack"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e503ccec-f1a0-3adf-8b3e-57bcae007295",
                                        "entry_id": "18bd51ad-7ae4-3186-8b9c-f77a1d62a82f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kind of loose-fitting gown or dress with sleeves which hangs from the shoulders, such as a gown with a Watteau back or sack-back, fashionable in the late 17th to 18th century; or, formerly, a loose-fitting hip-length jacket, cloak or cape."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a0e6725-2082-4457-a596-f92ab25d0240",
                                                "sense_id": "e503ccec-f1a0-3adf-8b3e-57bcae007295",
                                                "text": "Molly, therefore, having dressed herself out in this sack, with a new laced cap, and some other ornaments which Tom had given her, repairs to church with her fan in her hand the very next Sunday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccaeb397-4cef-4504-9433-6667ef0a9f62",
                                                "sense_id": "e503ccec-f1a0-3adf-8b3e-57bcae007295",
                                                "text": "Her Dress, too, was of the same cast, a thin muslin short sacque and Coat lined throughout with Pink, – a modesty bit – and something of a very short cloak half concealed about half of her old wrinkled Neck […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "482867e5-2992-4aca-8a28-5da27426faf9",
                                                "sense_id": "e503ccec-f1a0-3adf-8b3e-57bcae007295",
                                                "text": "This lady's interesting figure, on her wedding-day, was attired in a sacque and petticoat of the most expensive brocaded white silk, resembling net-work, enriched with small flowers […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0bc61f10-ae18-3a72-8bfc-185da3a3fd23",
                                        "entry_id": "18bd51ad-7ae4-3186-8b9c-f77a1d62a82f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sack coat; a kind of coat worn by men, and extending from top to bottom without a cross seam."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc3aed28-97c6-37b9-a0af-f7c60f79b4b2",
                                        "entry_id": "18bd51ad-7ae4-3186-8b9c-f77a1d62a82f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The scrotum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7a83f2a-c4d1-44fe-a397-ba1b5dcd2c29",
                                                "sense_id": "dc3aed28-97c6-37b9-a0af-f7c60f79b4b2",
                                                "text": "He got passed the ball, but it hit him in the sack."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
